WEBVTT

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.980
<b>Win 
the 
Idol Festival!!</b>

00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:32.990
This is our new song 
that goes on sale today.

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:35.690
<b>I-1 Club performs its new song!!</b>

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:35.690
It's by Hayasaka-san.

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:37.750
It's a very difficult song.

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:42.490
<b>Win 
the 
Idol Festival!!</b>

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:40.390
The choreography is incredibly challenging.

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:42.490
But that's what makes it worth doing.

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:45.500
This is "First-Rate Smile"!

00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:48.220
That's that.

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:52.030
I-1 released our song on CD?

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:53.490
I can't believe him.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:55.720
That's pretty messed up.

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:58.680
Could he have been a spy for I-1?

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:01.840
If I-1 releases that song on CD,

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:03.880
does that mean we can't sing it anymore?

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:07.120
Good point. There'd be copyright issues.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:08.970
President, do we have a contract?

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:11.490
Of course not.

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:14.070
That eccentric really got us this time.

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:17.570
Let's have him take responsibility for this.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:18.860
You're right.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:21.090
How do you want to do this?

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:22.840
Huh? What?

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:24.080
Well, in my day...

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.450
Seriously, what are we going to do?

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:31.440
I'm not sure we have enough 
time to learn a new song.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.010
But if we sing that at the finals,

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:37.090
we'll be singing in front of the I-1 Club.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.470
I definitely don't want to do that.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:40.910
Yeah, neither do I.

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:42.850
Congratulations.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:45.690
I don't know what miracle happened,

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:47.470
but I heard you made it 
through the preliminaries.

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:49.710
Bastard!

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:51.500
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait!

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:52.980
Get out of the way, Matsuda!

00:02:55.480 --> 00:03:01.490
I thought of an even better song, 
so I gave that one to I-1.

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:02.610
What?

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:07.030
I don't understand 
your thinking at all.

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:10.280
You can't help that. 
You're an ordinary person.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.750
See? Isn't this one way better?

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:18.510
This time, I'm going to have 
you sign a contract first.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.130
When I heard you made it 
through the preliminaries,

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:24.210
I had a thought, too.

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:26.100
It's time to really do this.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:29.570
Does this mean you've just been 
doing this for fun until now?

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:31.310
No, I've been serious the whole time.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:35.520
But now I guess I'm mega-serious.

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:37.050
You expect us to perform

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:40.190
a new song at the finals 
with so little time to prepare?

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:43.970
That's right. I told you, 
I'm tera-serious.

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:44.780
He's getting more serious...

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:47.990
If you win the Idol Festival,

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:51.540
you'll be officially recognized as I-1's rival.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:55.290
You could even say it would 
make you a top idol group.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:04:00.830
Top idols can learn new songs 
and choreography in a day.

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:04.800
If you can't do that, 
you won't last long in this industry.

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:08.630
Are you saying we'll win if we can do this?

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:10.940
That's up to you girls.

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:12.810
Oh, by the way...

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:15.680
This song's center is Nanase Yoshino.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:16.060
What?

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:18.320
It's you.

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:19.720
Me?

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:21.670
That's great, Yoppi.

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:22.910
It's your first time being the center.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:24.220
We're counting on you.

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:25.320
Okay.

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:27.830
Do your best to put something together.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:32.080
<b>Win 
the 
Idol Festival!!</b>

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:32.080
That's easier said than done.

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:34.970
It's so high pitched.

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:38.200
It's up-tempo, too. 
The choreography's probably difficult.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:39.460
You're right.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:59.230
<b>Win 
the 
Idol Festival!!</b>

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:43.770
I just learned a new song, 
and now I have to start all over.

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:45.900
I don't know if I can do this.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:47.700
But we have to do it.

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.040
There's less than a month before the finals.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:51.890
Are we going to be okay?

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:53.520
We'll make it okay.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:54.980
That's the spirit!

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:56.800
A lot has happened until now,

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:59.230
but we managed to overcome all obstacles!

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:02.150
All that's left to do is 
overcome the walls before us!

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:04.890
If we can't go over it, 
we'll break through!

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:06.210
If we can make it through this test,

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:09.240
I'm sure we'll find something 
new on the other side!

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:10.740
What's gotten into you?

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.080
I'm going to start calling you Shuzo.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.590
You're smothering us, Matsuda.

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:16.420
<b>Win 
the 
Idol Festival!!</b>

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:17.220
But it's the finals!

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:20.420
I feel like I can almost see the top...

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:25.630
<b>Idol Festival 
@ I-1 Arena</b>

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:25.630
We'll be in Tokyo this time next month.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:31.760
Hayasaka-sensei gave us another tough song.

00:05:32.290 --> 00:05:33.870
I wonder if you'll be all right.

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:35.140
We'll make it all right.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:40.260
It's even harder than I thought.

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:42.900
And it uses so much stamina.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:46.020
If we're this beat just from dancing,

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:48.410
we'll be in trouble when we add singing.

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:50.200
We need to be stronger.

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:51.910
We need more endurance.

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:56.490
If we can't sing while running for 
four or five minutes, we won't last.

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:00.000
Let's stretch harder, too.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.350
You're more prone to injury 
if your body's not flexible.

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:05.170
She's so inflexible...

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:07.450
Let's return to basics.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:12.430
<b>Idol Festival 
@ I-1 Arena</b>

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:12.430
Three more weeks.

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:24.140
Honestly, I think this 
song is really difficult,

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:28.740
but don't tell me you 
can't sing or dance this.

00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:30.990
Moeka, focus.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:34.210
Who? Me? I'm focusing.

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:37.700
Mai-Mai's saying something 
because that's not what it looks like.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:39.810
If you're going to make excuses 
or you really can't do it,

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:41.350
just get out of here.

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:44.750
Let's do it one more time.

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:47.260
She doesn't need to be so angry.

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:51.050
There must be a lot of 
pressure on the center.

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:52.640
She's got a lot riding on her shoulders.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.970
You say that, but you want her position.

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:57.440
Don't say that.

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:01.640
You can't, because I'm going 
to be the next center.

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:04.520
I won't let anyone else have it!

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:06.530
Okay, okay.

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:09.600
Wake Up, Girls! made it through 
the preliminaries, right?

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:12.090
Yeah. I texted Mayushi,

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:13.920
and she said she'll do her best at the finals.

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:16.200
If she didn't, we couldn't crush her.

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:19.570
Crush her? You don't 
have to put it like that.

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:24.540
It won't be much of a contest 
if they don't try to crush us, too.

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:28.520
But we're not competing directly.

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:33.010
If we're standing on the same stage, 
we'll be compared.

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:36.500
People will judge which of us did better.

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:38.520
You have a point.

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:40.910
Besides, have you heard about the new song?

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:42.010
What?

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:47.270
Hayasaka-san originally wrote 
that for Wake Up, Girls!.

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:49.570
They sang it at the regional preliminaries.

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:54.850
Which means people who heard it 
will be forced to compare us to them.

00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:56.070
That's right.

00:07:56.070 --> 00:07:58.420
Let's try to be friends.

00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:00.500
There's no reason for us to fight.

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:02.150
You're so naïve, Megu.

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:04.480
Don't you think you're 
worrying about it too much?

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:06.100
Who cares about that?

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:09.460
Anyway, did Hayasaka-san 
take their song away from them?

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:12.090
That'd be so sad for them.

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:13.100
Isn't it the other way around?

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:13.970
What?

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:16.460
They don't need it anymore.

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:19.470
I'm sure they'll bring something 
even more amazing to the finals.

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:23.230
I don't want to lose.

00:08:24.380 --> 00:08:28.540
Fortune and misfortune 
exist in this world,

00:08:28.990 --> 00:08:30.970
but they don't apply when 
accomplishing something

00:08:30.970 --> 00:08:32.470
with your own strength.

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:35.740
Misfortune is simply an excuse.

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:40.760
Online Poll Rankings

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:40.760
How high will their 
strength take them?

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:44.710
I got tickets!

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:49.890
Seats 51 to 65 in Block A2!

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:53.530
I was able to acquire 
some other good seats, as well!

00:08:53.530 --> 00:08:57.760
You can't get any closer 
than front row seats!

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:01.470
This is great start for fans of WUG like us!

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:03.290
Yeah!

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:06.800
I propose we display a level 
of restraint appropriate to WUG fans

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:10.040
so as not to cause discomfort 
for other audience members

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:13.360
or the members of WUG themselves 
due to these excellent seats!

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:15.000
Yeah!

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:15.790
A display of support

00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:18.250
is expected to take place in front 
of the stadium the day of the event!

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:19.990
I believe we should control 
ourselves there, as well!

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:21.830
Yeah!

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:24.750
Also, don't bring perishable gifts.

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:28.980
Let's discuss our plans beforehand, 
so we don't bring the same thing!

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:29.750
<b><<WUG Member Favorite Foods>> 

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:30.290
Yeah!

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:33.190
We can't compete with I-1 fans 
when it comes to numbers,

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:37.600
but no can beat our passion 
for Wake Up, Girls!!

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:38.760
Let's give it everything we have!

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:40.300
Yeah!

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:42.310
Could you please be quiet?

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:45.020
S-Sorry...

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:46.520
<b>Idol Festival 
@ I-1 Arena</b>

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:51.270
What's wrong, President?

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:56.030
The god of chance only has bangs, huh?

00:09:56.750 --> 00:09:59.190
What's with the dusky mood?

00:09:59.190 --> 00:10:01.090
It's not like you.

00:10:01.090 --> 00:10:02.160
Matsuda.

00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:03.350
Yes?

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:12.170
This idol group I formed 
on a whim seems

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:15.670
to have taken on a life of its own.

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:19.000
Well, I suppose so.

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:23.470
This may be a long shot, but...

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:25.180
No, don't.

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:26.640
Pride and peace.

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:28.530
These are the words 
that ruin creators.

00:10:28.530 --> 00:10:29.850
Don't let down your guard.

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:32.560
Anyway...

00:10:34.540 --> 00:10:37.020
A contract for a new office? When?

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:38.570
Time to sign.

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:40.840
Wait, wait, wait!

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:42.700
Are you sure you should do that?

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:47.470
I'm sure you all know,

00:10:47.470 --> 00:10:51.490
but we're going to the finals 
of the Idol Festival!

00:10:51.490 --> 00:10:52.920
Yeah!

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:59.550
A lot has happened, but we only 
made it this far because of you.

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:04.210
Thank you so, so much.

00:11:04.210 --> 00:11:07.250
Miyu, don't you think 
it's too early for that?

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:08.320
That's right.

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:10.660
Let's not shed tears until we win.

00:11:10.660 --> 00:11:11.560
Just kidding.

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:13.090
Yeah, yeah!

00:11:13.090 --> 00:11:17.460
Since we've made it this far, 
we'll definitely win.

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:18.690
You can do it!

00:11:19.290 --> 00:11:22.320
Thank you. We'll bring 
back that big trophy.

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:24.000
We'll be waiting for you!

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:30.340
Mayushi, have you been 
getting enough sleep?

00:11:30.340 --> 00:11:31.940
Not really.

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:34.580
We've been so busy lately.

00:11:36.760 --> 00:11:38.090
Hey, listen...

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:43.340
Could I get your autograph?

00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:44.490
What?

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:48.180
You advanced to the finals 
of the Idol Festival, right?

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:50.610
Does this mean you're 
being recruited for work?

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:53.350
My brother's really into it.

00:11:56.520 --> 00:12:01.360
For better or for worse or for giggles, 
today is your last lesson.

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:02.360
Yes, sir!

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:05.870
Show me the result of your practice.

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:12.250
<i>Here we go</i>

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:13.040
<i>We can do it</i>

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:14.520
<i>Wake Up, Girls!</i>

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:18.890
<i>Leave it up to us, everyone</i>

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:25.310
<i>We'll eat up your problems, 
no matter how heavy</i>

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:38.010
Two points, three points, 
three points, four points.

00:12:38.010 --> 00:12:41.260
Shouldn't you boost their 
confidence with good scores?

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:43.780
No, this is for real now.

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:45.340
Two points for your singing.

00:12:45.340 --> 00:12:46.420
Three points for your dancing.

00:12:46.420 --> 00:12:47.650
Three points for teamwork.

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:48.900
Four points for stamina.

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:50.040
That's 12 points total.

00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:54.870
You barely pass.

00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:58.790
Oh, each category is out of five points.

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:03.130
By the way, this is the first 
time I've awarded four points.

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:03.800
Clap, clap.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:05.550
We scored four points for stamina?

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:09.270
In just a few months, 
my lumpy potatoes have become

00:13:09.270 --> 00:13:15.560
piping hot potatoes parmentier 
or a chilled vichyssoise.

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:19.310
At a star-less restaurant, of course.

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:21.020
There's the malice.

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:22.320
I'm going to call you Ariyoshi.

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:29.540
The score I gave you 
isn't your true score, of course.

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:35.020
Now it's up to you to entertain 
as many fans as possible

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:37.020
at the I-1 Arena at the finals,

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:39.320
from the ones in the very front 
to the ones in the very back

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:41.840
to the fans on the second and third

00:13:42.310 --> 00:13:45.230
floor seats who think you look this big.

00:13:45.230 --> 00:13:49.150
In that respect, there's no 
such thing as a passing score.

00:13:49.150 --> 00:13:52.540
The truth is, no matter how hard you try,

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:55.360
there's no such thing as a perfect score.

00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:59.100
Pursuing that perfect score 
is what it means to be an idol.

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:00.610
Also...

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:04.280
I'm not the one whose recognition you need.

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:05.810
It's the audience.

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:12.990
I-I'll make you acknowledge me someday.

00:14:14.390 --> 00:14:17.460
My acknowledgment won't do you any good.

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:18.870
Yes, sir!

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:23.040
Huh? I think Hayasaka-san's 
words moved me.

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:25.130
What is this strange feeling?

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:27.380
He's no ordinary man.

00:14:27.890 --> 00:14:29.890
Thank you very much!

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:33.390
Anyway, I'm going to get some beef tongue.

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:34.350
Who's coming with me?

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:36.690
I'll go! I'll go!

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:37.890
Are you paying, Hayasaka-san?

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:40.910
What? Why would I pay for you?

00:14:40.910 --> 00:14:43.900
Because you're the wealthiest one here.

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:47.090
No, no. Don't be such hyenas.

00:14:47.090 --> 00:14:50.600
What? They say money 
makes the world go round.

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:53.910
If you don't make it turn, 
we'll never get ours.

00:14:55.860 --> 00:14:57.450
It's finally tomorrow.

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:58.790
Let's do our best.

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:00.950
You just wait, Tokyo.

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:02.050
Anyway...

00:15:04.330 --> 00:15:05.400
I brought these.

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:08.030
Scrunchies? Did you make them?

00:15:08.030 --> 00:15:08.800
Yeah.

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:12.300
Thanks, Yoppi.

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:14.590
How cute.

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:15.340
They're so cute.

00:15:15.340 --> 00:15:17.060
Way to go, leader.

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:21.310
Mayu.

00:15:21.910 --> 00:15:22.980
Here.

00:15:23.350 --> 00:15:24.080
Huh?

00:15:25.170 --> 00:15:29.090
The weather report said 
it's cold in Tokyo this year.

00:15:29.560 --> 00:15:30.820
Thanks.

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:33.570
Do your best.

00:15:33.100 --> 00:15:33.570
I will.

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:39.330
<b>Squid Shiokara Kesennuma</b>

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:37.960
Yeah, I know.

00:15:37.960 --> 00:15:39.330
That's my plan.

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:47.340
<b>Shark Fin Curry</b>

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:47.340
<b>Patteku EX 
Cold Compress</b>

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:47.340
<b>Cold Capsules DX</b>

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:47.340
<b>Tsukimi Soba</b>

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:42.300
What? Medicine?

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:44.350
I'll take what you sent me.

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:47.350
Um, listen...

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:53.090
Thanks for everything, Auntie.

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:12.420
I'm coming in.

00:16:12.420 --> 00:16:14.190
Okay.

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:18.870
Mom said you should take these.

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:20.870
What? All of these?

00:16:21.610 --> 00:16:23.470
You're so cool, Nee-chan.

00:16:23.470 --> 00:16:24.580
Really?

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:27.400
Yeah. I bragged to everyone about you.

00:16:31.220 --> 00:16:34.280
Maybe Harajuku and Akiba.

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:37.510
I hope I have time.

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:41.770
Let's toast to Minami-chan 
advancing to the finals.

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:44.120
Cheers!

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:56.780
<b>You can do it, Minami-chan!</b>

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:47.830
I wish we could go to Tokyo to support you.

00:16:47.830 --> 00:16:48.990
It's okay.

00:16:48.990 --> 00:16:52.520
Matsuda-san's going to film it. 
I'll show you when I get back.

00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:55.030
I hope you win.

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:56.780
I will win.

00:16:56.780 --> 00:16:59.780
That's why I've been practicing.

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:11.050
I need to keep it together.

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:14.390
Are you running away from home?

00:17:14.390 --> 00:17:15.930
You're one to talk.

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:17.030
Huh?

00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:18.810
Your luggage is impressive.

00:17:18.810 --> 00:17:23.930
What? But I need clothes 
for Harajuku, Shibuya, and Akiba.

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:26.170
We're not going to have fun.

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:29.120
You're right.

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:30.690
Give that back!

00:17:57.860 --> 00:18:00.400
Tokyo's so crowded.

00:18:00.400 --> 00:18:01.910
And scary.

00:18:01.910 --> 00:18:03.530
I'm already exhausted.

00:18:03.530 --> 00:18:05.230
Don't let them underestimate you.

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:06.980
Underestimate who?

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:09.970
We've got rehearsal 
at the arena this afternoon.

00:18:09.970 --> 00:18:12.250
We'll leave as soon as we drop off our luggage.

00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:14.190
What's wrong?

00:18:14.770 --> 00:18:16.450
Why are you so scared?

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:19.490
Half of all people in Tokyo 
are from the countryside.

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:21.140
What? You're worried about that?

00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:25.180
Not only that, but hardly anyone's 
a third generation Tokyo resident.

00:18:25.180 --> 00:18:26.700
Half?

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:27.630
Really?

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:29.250
What? You're happy with that?

00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:33.000
What's wrong?

00:18:35.490 --> 00:18:37.590
I think I'm a little nervous.

00:18:42.460 --> 00:18:43.680
This is it.

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:46.080
Let's head inside.

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:47.020
Follow me.

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:56.030
Tohoku Block Representatives

00:18:57.260 --> 00:18:58.890
First, there's an explanation of the arena.

00:18:58.890 --> 00:19:01.130
After that, it's the sound 
and light rehearsal.

00:19:01.130 --> 00:19:02.780
The performance starts at 6 PM.

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:04.160
It's huge!

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:06.630
How many people does this place hold?

00:19:06.630 --> 00:19:08.020
27,000!

00:19:08.020 --> 00:19:09.960
That's a hundred Macanas!

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:11.870
Don't get swallowed up, WUG!

00:19:11.870 --> 00:19:13.670
All right! Let's practice our cheer!

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:15.420
Yeah!

00:19:16.230 --> 00:19:21.500
Maybe it's ten... no, a hundred 
times bigger than Macana.

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:22.630
Yeah.

00:19:22.630 --> 00:19:25.180
A bunch of people are coming in here.

00:19:26.330 --> 00:19:27.930
It's amazing.

00:19:28.360 --> 00:19:31.780
I wonder if they'll hear 
us in such a big place.

00:19:31.780 --> 00:19:34.250
We'll be using mics, 
so don't worry about that.

00:19:34.250 --> 00:19:37.940
But we might want to make 
our dancing more dynamic.

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:38.920
Yeah.

00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:41.580
Yoppi?

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:43.000
I'm fine.

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:45.200
We just have to do 
what we've been doing.

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:47.070
Please get off the stage.

00:19:47.070 --> 00:19:48.700
The I-1 Club's coming in.

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:53.150
Watch out!

00:19:53.150 --> 00:19:54.620
Sorry.

00:19:54.620 --> 00:19:55.710
Are you okay?

00:19:57.610 --> 00:19:59.110
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:19:59.110 --> 00:20:00.240
You sure?

00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:01.050
Yeah.

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:05.780
Excuse me. I believe it's 
written on the schedule,

00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:08.520
but the I-1 Club 
has a live TV appearance.

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:10.730
They'll be doing their tech rehearsal first.

00:20:11.360 --> 00:20:12.520
Mayu!

00:20:13.720 --> 00:20:14.810
Megumi!

00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:17.590
Are you leaving right after this?

00:20:17.590 --> 00:20:20.660
If you have time, do you want 
to get something to eat?

00:20:20.660 --> 00:20:22.350
Sure, yeah.

00:20:22.350 --> 00:20:23.240
You came.

00:20:25.550 --> 00:20:27.990
I told you before, but come 
at us with everything you have.

00:20:28.440 --> 00:20:29.490
I know.

00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:42.260
That center never changes.

00:20:44.540 --> 00:20:46.550
Thanks for working with us!

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:56.060
<i>A schedule written in the clouds</i>

00:20:56.060 --> 00:20:58.900
<i>Filling an empty weekend</i>

00:20:59.370 --> 00:21:05.660
<i>With anything you can isn't right</i>

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:09.280
<i>Only truly plain and ordinary days</i>

00:21:09.280 --> 00:21:12.920
<i>I film videos of my cat</i>

00:21:12.260 --> 00:21:13.920
They're amazing.

00:21:12.920 --> 00:21:18.330
<i>Maybe I'll try redecorating 
my room sometime</i>

00:21:13.920 --> 00:21:15.290
They're the best.

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:21.780
<i>I made a slideshow...</i>

00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:24.390
I wouldn't expect any less from I-1.

00:21:24.820 --> 00:21:27.050
That doesn't sound like a compliment.

00:21:27.490 --> 00:21:29.250
It is.

00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:32.350
But if you're asking 
if I think it's interesting...

00:21:33.720 --> 00:21:36.490
Lights and sound. 
Does everything look okay?

00:21:37.290 --> 00:21:39.340
Good work, everyone.

00:21:39.340 --> 00:21:41.320
Thank you!

00:21:43.380 --> 00:21:48.270
Finalists, gather back here in 30 minutes.

00:21:48.270 --> 00:21:49.070
Yes, sir!

00:21:49.530 --> 00:21:51.050
It's finally here.

00:21:51.490 --> 00:21:52.780
It's almost time.

00:21:52.780 --> 00:21:55.330
I'm so nervous, I feel like my 
heart's going to leap out of my chest.

00:21:55.700 --> 00:21:57.170
Show me.

00:21:57.170 --> 00:21:58.500
It's just an expression!

00:22:11.970 --> 00:22:14.970
To be continued

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:47.460
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:45.310 --> 00:23:46.900
The next episode is the last one.

00:23:46.900 --> 00:23:48.480
You're kidding. How sad.

00:23:48.480 --> 00:23:50.620
One season's surprisingly short.

00:23:50.620 --> 00:23:52.560
I hope I didn't forget 
to do anything.

00:23:52.560 --> 00:23:53.880
I hope we get a second season.

00:23:53.880 --> 00:23:54.990
I'll do this!

00:23:54.990 --> 00:23:56.850
The last episode's really tasty, meow!

00:23:56.850 --> 00:24:00.250
The next episode is 
"No Regrets in this Moment!"

00:23:56.850 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>"No Regrets in this Moment"</b>

00:24:00.250 --> 00:24:02.250
<b></b>

00:24:02.250 --> 00:24:04.250
<b></b>
